<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Emirate of Diriyah</h1><p class="st-meta">1727 CE – 1818 CE · capital Diriyah</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first Saudi state, born of an alliance between the Al Saud and the reformer Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab, which conquered most of Arabia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-saud">Muhammad ibn Saud</a> became emir of the small oasis town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diriyah">Diriyah</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Najd</a> in 1727. In 1744 he made a pact with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-abd-al-wahhab">Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab</a>, a preacher calling for a return to strict <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monotheism">monotheism</a>: the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-saud">Al Saud</a> would support the reform movement, and the scholar would legitimise their rule.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> expanded by war and conversion, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riyadh">Riyadh</a> in 1773, defeating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/banu-khalid-emirate">Banu Khalid Emirate</a> and conquering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-ahsa-oasis">al-Hasa</a>. It collected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zakat">zakat</a> from subject towns and tribes and destroyed shrines seen as idolatrous. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saud-ibn-abd-al-aziz">Saud ibn Abd al-Aziz</a> its forces sacked Karbala in 1802 and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> in 1803 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a> soon after, and raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> sent the army of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/egypt-under-muhammad-ali">Egypt under Muhammad Ali</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibrahim-pasha-of-egypt">Ibrahim Pasha</a> besieged and destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diriyah">Diriyah</a> in 1818; the last emir, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-ibn-saud">Abdullah ibn Saud</a>, was executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a>. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-nejd">Emirate of Nejd</a> revived Saudi rule in 1824. The ruins of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/at-turaif">al-Turaif</a> are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">World Heritage Site</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/emirate-of-diriyah.jpg" alt="Emirate of Diriyah" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: David First · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_First_and_Second_Saudi_State_(1744-1891).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1727 CE – 1818 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Diriyah</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Muhammad ibn Saud, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, Saud ibn Abd al-Aziz</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam (Wahhabi)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a>, <a href="/countries/qatar">Qatar</a>, <a href="/countries/bahrain">Bahrain</a>, <a href="/countries/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>First Saudi State, Diriyah Emirate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1772&amp;focus=emirate-of-diriyah" aria-label="Emirate of Diriyah on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5917 1267 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Emirate of Diriyah lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path cla